@startuml provider_identity_model
title Provider Identity and Runtime Contract

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: Provider, MutableModels, ModelsImpl, and createProvider
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/types.ts: ProviderId, Model, SimpleStreamOptions, and ToolChoice
' Observed behavior: provider.id is the registry key and Model.provider selects the owning provider.
' Design reason: provider identity, protocol dispatch, model identity, and connection configuration remain separate.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
  ArrowColor #475569
}

class ProviderIdentity {
  +providerId: string
}

class ProviderRuntimeContract {
  +displayName: string
  +auth: ProviderAuth.none
  +getModels(): Model[]
  +refreshModels(): optional
  +stream(model, context, options)
}

class ModelIdentity {
  +providerId: string
  +modelId: string
}

class ModelDescriptor {
  +modelId: string
  +apiId: internal string
  +capabilities
  +limits
  +cost
}

class ApiProtocol {
  +configuredApiId: openai-completions
  +request and SSE implementation
}

ProviderIdentity "1" *-- "1" ProviderRuntimeContract : identifies
ProviderIdentity "1" *-- "0..*" ModelIdentity : owns
ModelIdentity "1" *-- "1" ModelDescriptor : describes
ModelDescriptor --> ApiProtocol : internal dispatch
ProviderRuntimeContract --> ApiProtocol : fixed by configuration

note right of ProviderIdentity
Only providerId determines identity.
Name, URL, credentials, and apiId
do not participate in identity.
end note

note bottom of ModelIdentity
Runtime model key is
(providerId, modelId).
end note
@enduml

@startuml generic_provider_boundary
title Generic CampusMate Chat Provider Boundary

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: ModelsImpl.requireProvider and stream
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-completions.ts: stream, convertMessages, and usage parsing
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/CampusClawAiService.java: resolveProvider
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAICompletionsProvider.java: buildParams and parseUsage
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/application.yml:89-108
' mate-service src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/agentdefinition/modelmanager/controller/LlmChatController.java:35-55
' Architecture change: Java resolves an AiProvider by model.providerId and uses an internally configured apiId.
' Observed behavior: mate-service implements POST /mate-service/v1/LLM/chat at baseline 956b547f.
' Architecture change: all clients read one campusmate tree with a shared base URL and endpoint catalog.
' Architecture change: target model options bind to campusmate.model, not campusmate.model-manager.
' Product constraint: CampusClaw and Mate exchange no application identity or credential headers.
' Scope boundary: Mate routing, credentials, and upstream field adaptation are internal Mate concerns.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

package "pi-mono-java Runtime" {
  [CampusMate Service Configuration\ncampusmate.base-url\ncampusmate.endpoints\ncampusmate.model] as CampusMateConfig
  [AgentLoop] as Loop
  [CampusClawAiService] as AiService
  [AiProviderRegistry] as Registry
  [MateServiceModelManagerProvider\nproviderId = mate-model-manager\nauth = none] as GenericProvider
  [ManagedModelCatalogClient] as CatalogClient
  [ManagedModelInvocationClient] as InvocationClient
  database "t_session_entries\nt_session_records\nt_session_stats" as SessionStore
}

package "mate-service" {
  [Internal Model Catalog API] as CatalogApi
  [Mate Chat Endpoint\n/mate-service/v1/LLM/chat] as ChatApi
  [Mate Model Routing] as Router
}

cloud "Upstream LLM Services" as Vendors
[Internal Gateway Trust Boundary] as Gateway

Loop --> AiService : model + Context + options
AiService --> Registry : get(model.providerId)
Registry --> GenericProvider
GenericProvider --> CatalogClient
GenericProvider --> InvocationClient
CampusMateConfig --> CatalogClient : shared origin and paths
CampusMateConfig --> InvocationClient : shared origin and model Chat path
GenericProvider --> SessionStore : usage projection owned by Runtime
CatalogClient --> Gateway : HTTPS JSON and protocol headers
InvocationClient --> Gateway : Mate Chat JSON and SSE
Gateway --> CatalogApi : no app identity or credentials
Gateway --> ChatApi : no app identity or credentials
ChatApi --> Router : validated Mate modelId and request
Router --> Vendors : Mate-owned upstream invocation

note bottom of GenericProvider
The Runtime sees one provider and opaque Mate modelIds.
The internal apiId defaults to openai-completions.
The HTTP request never carries apiId or credentials.
end note
@enduml

@startuml model_manager_invocation_sequence
title CampusMate Foreground Chat Invocation and Disconnect Cancellation

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-completions.ts: stream, convertMessages, tool calls, and usage parsing
' pi-mono packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts: runLoop and streamAssistantResponse
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/compaction/compaction.ts: completeSummarization with toolChoice none
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAICompletionsProvider.java: stream and parseUsage
' pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java: invokeModel and consumeStream
' mate-service src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/agentdefinition/modelmanager/controller/LlmChatController.java:35-55
' Observed behavior: POST /mate-service/v1/LLM/chat exists in the analyzed mate-service baseline.
' Product constraint: cancellation closes the foreground request and has no separate cancel operation.
' Architecture change: successful Chat SSE is returned without ResultBean or payload rewriting.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor Client
participant "AgentLoop" as Loop
participant "CampusClawAiService" as AiService
participant "AiProviderRegistry" as Registry
participant "MateServiceModelManagerProvider" as Provider
participant "Internal Gateway" as Gateway
participant "mate-service Chat Endpoint" as Mate
participant "Upstream LLM" as Upstream

Client -> Loop : submit prompt
Loop -> AiService : stream(model, Context, options)
AiService -> Registry : get(model.providerId)
Registry --> AiService : Mate provider
AiService -> Provider : streamSimple(model, Context, options)
Provider -> Provider : validate text-only context
Provider -> Provider : map Context to messages, tools, and options
Provider -> Gateway : POST /mate-service/v1/LLM/chat\nprotocol headers only
Gateway -> Mate : trusted internal route\nno app identity or credentials
Mate -> Upstream : Mate-owned invocation

loop Raw OpenAI-style Chat SSE
  Upstream --> Mate : data chunk
  Mate --> Gateway : unchanged success chunk
  Gateway --> Provider : unchanged success chunk
  Provider -> Provider : map text, reasoning, tool calls, and usage
  Provider --> Loop : AssistantMessageEvent
end

alt Normal completion
  Upstream --> Mate : data: [DONE]
  Mate --> Provider : data: [DONE]
  Provider --> Loop : final AssistantMessage
else Caller aborts
  Loop -> Provider : cancel subscription
  Provider -> Gateway : close request and SSE body
  Gateway -> Mate : downstream disconnect
  Mate -> Upstream : abort or close upstream request
  Provider --> Loop : StopReason.ABORTED
else Error before SSE starts
  Mate --> Provider : HTTP error and ResultBean
  Provider --> Loop : StopReason.ERROR
else Error after SSE starts
  Mate --> Provider : event: error then close
  Provider --> Loop : StopReason.ERROR
end

note over Provider,Mate
No create POST replay after an unknown outcome.
No responseId-based cancel request exists.
Tool execution stays in AgentLoop.
Mate upstream adaptation is outside this contract.
end note
@enduml

@startuml java_provider_alignment
title Java Provider Alignment with pi-mono

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/models.ts: Provider and Models registry keyed by provider.id
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/api/openai-completions.ts: Chat conversion and stream processing
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/ApiProviderRegistry.java: registry keyed by Api
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAICompletionsProvider.java: current Chat mapper
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/Provider.java: closed enum with CUSTOM
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/application.yml:89-140, three CampusMate address keys
' Java divergence: the initial d649866a6 baseline models protocol adapters as providers and cannot preserve arbitrary provider identity.
' Architecture change: add open ProviderId and ApiId values, resolve AiProvider by providerId, and configure apiId internally.
' Architecture change: Model Manager, Runtime, and Tool clients share one campusmate tree and endpoint catalog.
' Architecture change: model options bind to campusmate.model while component and provider names remain stable.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
  ArrowColor #475569
}

package "Initial Java Baseline d649866a6" {
  enum ProviderEnum
  enum ApiEnum
  class ModelCurrent
  interface ApiProvider
  class ApiProviderRegistryCurrent
  ModelCurrent --> ProviderEnum
  ModelCurrent --> ApiEnum
  ApiProviderRegistryCurrent --> ApiProvider : keyed by ApiEnum
}

package "Target Java" {
  class ProviderId
  class ApiId
  class ModelTarget
  interface AiProvider
  class AiProviderRegistry
  interface ProtocolAdapter
  class ProtocolAdapterRegistry
  class ProviderAuthNone
  class MateServiceModelManagerProvider
  class OpenAICompletionsMapper
  class CampusMateBaseUrlConfig
  class CampusMateEndpointConfig
  class ModelManagerClientConfig {
    +prefix: campusmate.model
  }
  ModelTarget --> ProviderId
  ModelTarget --> ApiId
  AiProviderRegistry --> AiProvider : keyed by ProviderId
  AiProvider --> ProtocolAdapterRegistry : optional internal dispatch
  ProtocolAdapterRegistry --> ProtocolAdapter : keyed by ApiId
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider ..|> AiProvider
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider --> ProviderAuthNone : auth returns none
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider --> OpenAICompletionsMapper : Context and raw SSE mapping
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider --> CampusMateBaseUrlConfig : shared origin
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider --> CampusMateEndpointConfig : model Chat path
  MateServiceModelManagerProvider --> ModelManagerClientConfig : timeouts and apiId
}

ProviderEnum ..> ProviderId : deprecate enum boundary
ApiEnum ..> ApiId : preserve known constants
ApiProvider ..> ProtocolAdapter : rename responsibility
@enduml

@startuml token_usage_persistence
title Session Usage Records and Statistics

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/agent/src/harness/session/types.ts: UsageRecord and SessionStats
' pi-mono packages/session-backends/sqlite-node/src/sqlite/migrations/001_initial.sql: records and session_stats
' pi-mono packages/session-backends/sqlite-node/src/sqlite/repo.ts: appendRecord
' pi-mono packages/session-backends/sqlite-node/src/sqlite/storage/session-stats.ts: addUsageToStats
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/db/gaussdb/install/session_schema.sql: t_session_entries, t_session_sequences, and t_session_materialized
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java: assistantEntry and Usage.empty reconstruction
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java: appendLocked
' Observed behavior: current centralized Java persistence drops AssistantMessage usage and has no record or stats write path.
' Target-only design: add t_session_records and t_session_stats without changing the message branch leaf.
' Design reason: usage is an immutable execution fact and must not become a branchable conversation entry.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

[RuntimeEventProjector] as Projector
[RuntimeSessionRepository] as Repository
database "t_session_sequences\nshared next_seq" as Sequence
database "t_session_entries\nbranchable messages" as Entries
database "t_session_records\nimmutable usage records" as Records
database "t_session_stats\nmaterialized totals" as Stats
database "t_session_materialized\nnon-usage views" as Materialized

Projector --> Repository : assistant message and Usage
Repository --> Sequence : allocate two ordered sequence values
Repository --> Entries : insert Assistant Entry\nupdate active leaf
Repository --> Records : insert type = usage\ndo not update active leaf
Repository --> Stats : increment message and usage totals
Repository ..> Materialized : lifetimeUsage removed

note bottom of Repository
Assistant Entry, Usage Record, and Stats update
commit or roll back in one database transaction.
Missing upstream usage is stored as zero values,
matching the pi Usage contract.
end note
@enduml
